  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Where new code goes",
      "items": [
        "A new resource or data source is one resource_*.go or datasource_*.go file whose init() calls registerResource or registerDataSource; nothing else needs wiring",
        "A missing Lakekeeper endpoint becomes a new *api.Client method in internal/provider/api",
        "Warehouse schema and model conversions go in internal/provider/warehouse"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Import rule",
      "items": [
        "Only internal/provider/api may import the Lakekeeper Go SDK",
        "The depguard rule lakekeeper-sdk in .golangci.yml denies it in every other file; make lint fails on a violation",
        "Everything else uses *api.Client and the api types"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Naming trap",
      "items": [
        "Package sdk (internal/provider/sdk) is the assignment schema fragment, not the Lakekeeper Go SDK",
        "Warehouse module and assignment schema fragment import api for its types, never the SDK"
      ]
    }
  ]
